DevOps Interview Series | #GitLab CI Scenario Based Questions

A pipeline runs on every commit but should run only on merge requests. How do you fix it?

Secrets were accidentally exposed in job logs. What steps will you take immediately?

Pipeline execution is slow due to repeated dependency downloads. How do you optimize it?

Self-hosted runners frequently go offline. How do you troubleshoot and stabilize them?

You need manual approval before deploying to production. How will you implement it?

One job depends on output from another job. How do you share that data?

A pipeline works on main but fails on feature branches. How do you debug it?

You need different deployments for dev, stage, and prod. How do you design the pipeline?

Shared runners are overloaded. When
and how do you move to specific runners?

A third-party CI template breaks your pipeline. How do you protect against this?

You need to deploy to Kubernetes using GitLab CI. How will you design the pipeline?

A job fails only when triggered manually. How do you troubleshoot?

You want to restrict deployment jobs to protected branches only. How do you enforce it?

Multiple repositories require the same CI logic. How do you avoid duplication?

Security team asks for pipeline execution audit logs. How will you provide them?

You need rollback support for failed deployments. How will you implement it?

Pipeline jobs consume excessive CPU/memory. How do you control resource usage?

Secrets differ per environment. How do you manage them securely?

You need multi-cloud deployments from a single GitLab CI pipeline. How will you design it?

You are asked to replace GitLab CI. What limitations would you highlight?
